  <text xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.pythagorizoysa.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.pythagorizoysa.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.pythagorizoysa.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0402_pythagorizoysa"><head>ΠΥΘΑΓΟΡΙΖΟΥΣΑ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1">
              <head>I.</head>
              <quote>
                <lg>
                  <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1-l1">Ὕδατος ἀπέφθου κύαθον· ἂν δ᾿ ὠμὸν πίῃ,</l>
                  <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1-l2">βαρὺ καὶ κοπῶδες.</l>
                </lg>
              </quote>
              <note type="source">Athenaeus III p. 122 f: προπίνω σοι, ἔφη, φιλοτησίαν — παρ᾿ Ἀλέξιδος λαβὼν ἐκ Πυθαγοριζούσης Ὕδατος ἀπέφθου κτλ.</note>
              <note type="apparatus">Vs. 1 πίῃ VL. πίνῃ ABP.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2_3" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3">
              <head>II. III.</head>
              <quote>
                <lg>
                  <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l1">Ἡ δ᾿ ἑστίασις ἰσχάδες καὶ στέμφυλα</l>
                  <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l2">καὶ τυρὸς ἔσται· ταῦτα γὰρ θύειν νόμος</l>
                  <l n="3" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l3">τοῖς Πυθαγορείοις. <sp>
                      <speaker>Β.</speaker>
                      <l n="4" part="F" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l4">νὴ Δί᾿, ἱερεῖον μὲν οὖν</l>
                    </sp>
                  </l>
                </lg>
              </quote>
              <pb n="475" facs="urn:hathi:hvd.32044079388682:scan:481" />
              <lg>
                <l n="5" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l5">ὁποῖον ἂν κάλλιστον, ὦ βέλτιστ᾽, ἔχῃ.</l>
                <gap reason="lost" />
                <l n="6" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l6">Ἔδει δ᾽ ὑπομεῖναι μικροσιτίαν, ῥύπον,</l>
                <l n="7" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-2_3-l7">ῥῖγος, σιωπήν, στυγνότητ᾽, ἀλουσίαν.</l>
              </lg>
              <note type="source">Athenaeus IV p. 161 d. allatis Alexidis versibus ex Tarentinis: καὶ ἐν Πυθαγοριζούσῃ <quote>Ἡ δ᾽ ἑστίασις — ὦ βέλτιστ᾽ ἔχῃ</quote>. καὶ μετ᾽ ὀλίγα <quote>Ἔδει δ᾽ ὑπομεῖναι</quote> κτλ.</note>
              <note type="apparatus">Vs. 3 Πυθαγορείοις P. πυθαγορίοις AVL. — Vs. 4 ὁποῖον ἂν Casaubonus. ὁποῖον οὗ AP. ὁποιονοῦν VL. — Vs. 5 μικροσιτίαν Porsonus. Libri μικρὸν ἀσιτίαν. Respicit locum Eustathius p. 1560 60.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="4" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-4">
              <head>IV.</head>
              <note type="source">Gellius Noct. Att. IV 11: porculis quoque minusculis et haedis tenerioribus victitasse (Pythagoram) idem Aristoxenus refert. — Ac de animalibus Alexis etiam poeta in comoedia quae Pythagorizusa inscribitur, docet.</note>
              <note type="apparatus">Vid. Hist. crit. p. 390.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1_2" ana="#compiled-duplicate-number #compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1_2">
              <head>Ι.</head>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1_2-l1">Cape aquae decoctae cyathum: si crudam bibas</l>
                <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-1_2-l2">erit insalubre.</l>
              </lg>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="3" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-3">
              <head>III.</head>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-3-l1">Decuit tolerare paulum sordem, inediam,</l>
                <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-pythagorizoysa-3-l2">illuviem, frigus, tristitiam, silentium.</l>
              </lg>
            </div>
          </div></body></text></TEI>